Summary Report: I think using the A.I (chatgpt) was really nice because I always struggled with writing code and how to like translate it into c++ language, so for me to write the pesudocode and explain the logic to the a.i and it generates the code for you is very nice. One thing though is that a.i always forgets if you message too much because it depends on the context window, so like in the chat when I was doing the unit tests it completely forgot the functions it implemented in graph.cpp and it filp flopped the dump function thinking it prints from the bottom when it prints from the top was interesting. But its also mind blowing how much the a.i has improved because I remember back like couple years ago a.i couldn't solve like any coding problems and generate a.i slop, so seeing it actually generate good code that works is a big step in the right direction. Overall, the a.i did everything I expected it to, but the only complaint is the memory and how it forgets and then generates dumb stuff.







